<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Sabena names new chairman.</title>
<headline>Belgian Sabena names new chairman.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian national airline Sabena on Monday named Belgian Valere Croes as its new chairman, succeeding Jan Hughebaert who was appointed on a temporary basis last February after the resignation of Pierre Godfroid.</p>
<p>Godfroid quit after a dogfight with unions that threatened the future of Sabena, 49.5 percent owned by Swissair.</p>
<p>Croes is also chairman of Belgian ASLK/CGER Bank and board member of ASLK Insurance, Fortis AG, Metropolitan Bank and Tractebel. He is a member too of the supervisory board of Dutch-Belgian financial services group Fortis. He joined Sabena's board on September 11.</p>
